{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785173893,"nonce":"0x8Vm+U/CN0BSfa4zLR0g1/PFjg=","message":"Fixed on master (pushed to origin + github), two commits:\n\n  2e229eb review: hash diff content in series fingerprint when git patch-id is absent\n  0e4597b review: prefer message-id over fingerprint in find_existing_change_id\n\n**2e229eb — the fix.** `LoreSeries.fingerprint` now falls back to\n`LoreMessage.get_patchwork_hash(patch.body)` when a patch has a diff but\n`git_patch_id` is None (i.e. plain `diff -u` with no `diff --git` header, as\nRandy's series carry). This restores content-sensitivity to the fingerprint so\ndistinct same-author rev-1 series no longer collapse to\n`sha256(\"\u003cemail\u003e:\u003crevision\u003e\")`.\n\n**0e4597b — hardening (defense-in-depth).** `find_existing_change_id` now\nresolves message-ids in a first pass and only falls back to fingerprint\nmatching second. A message-id belongs to exactly one series, so a real msgid\nmatch must never lose to a colliding fingerprint. This alone would not have\nfixed the reported case, but it closes off the whole class of\nfingerprint-collision folding.\n\nTests: `src/tests/test_fingerprint.py` (redline: two distinct rdunlap rev-1\nseries must produce different fingerprints; asserts the has_diff=True /\ngit_patch_id=None preconditions) and a precedence test in\n`test_review_tracking.py::TestFindExistingChangeId`. Full ci.sh green\n(1229 passed) before landing.\n\nMarking in-testing pending confirmation from Mark against his setup.","files":null}]}